ready: 1
kind: rule
id: recall.rule.priority
display_id: RULE-RECALL-PRIORITY
module: recall
title: Which memories earn a place in working memory
summary: >-
  Decides which memories go into working memory first and fills the token budget in that order.
notes: >-
  Boot settings and the agent's identity come first; everything else is ordered by kind, strength,
  salience, relevance, and how often it helped.
inputs:
- name: candidates
  source: Active memories in the stack
  source_kind: stored
- name: usage
  source: Recall usage counts
  source_kind: stored
- name: relevance
  source: The relevance rule
  source_kind: derived
- name: budget
  source: The caller's budget, clamped
  source_kind: parameter
decision:
  nodes:
  - id: cand
    node_kind: input
    text: Active memories of the stack, excluding dormant, forgotten and superseded ones
    refs:
    - memory.data.memory
  - id: excl
    node_kind: decision
    text: Has the memory hurt more often than it helped by the exclusion margin?
    refs:
    - recall.data.usage
    - recall.const.hurt-exclusion-margin
  - id: out
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Left out of automatic recall but still searchable
  - id: first
    node_kind: action
    text: Reserve room for boot settings, the active self-narrative, values and foundational beliefs,
      then the latest checkpoint
    refs:
    - recall.data.boot-config
    - recall.data.checkpoint
    - identity.data.self-narrative
  - id: score
    node_kind: calc
    text: Score every other memory by kind weight, strength, salience, relevance and usage
    refs:
    - recall.const.type-weights
    - recall.rule.relevance
  - id: fill
    node_kind: decision
    text: Does the next memory fit the remaining budget?
  - id: add
    node_kind: action
    text: Add it, shortened at a word boundary when shortening is allowed
  - id: stop
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Stop and report how many memories were left out
  edges:
  - from: cand
    to: excl
  - from: excl
    to: out
    label: 'yes'
  - from: excl
    to: first
    label: 'no'
  - from: first
    to: score
  - from: score
    to: fill
  - from: fill
    to: add
    label: 'yes'
  - from: add
    to: fill
  - from: fill
    to: stop
    label: no, or none left
calculations:
- name: score
  expr: type_weight × (0.5 + 0.5 × strength) × (0.75 + 0.25 × salience) × relevance_factor ÷ (1 + max(0,
    hurt_count − helped_count))
- name: relevance_factor
  expr: 1 when no context or query is given, else 0.25 + 0.75 × relevance
- name: tokens
  expr: characters ÷ 4, rounded up
rules:
- recall.rule.relevance
constants:
- recall.const.type-weights
- recall.const.hurt-exclusion-margin
- recall.const.default-token-budget
- recall.const.min-token-budget
- recall.const.max-token-budget
rationale: Strength and salience are in the score so that use and emotion change what the agent carries
  into a session; a memory of a costly mistake outranks a routine note of the same kind. Identity and
  boot settings are reserved first because the agent's sense of itself should not depend on how busy its
  recent work was. A context or query narrows the load without excluding the identity core.
